<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adib Shishakli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a>–<a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adib Shishakli was a Syrian army officer who took part in the coups of 1949 and ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> as its military strongman from late 1949 to 1954, as president from 1953. His authoritarian rule provoked a revolt and a military rising that forced him into exile in 1954, after which parliamentary government returned. He was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in 1964.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adib-shishakli.jpg" alt="Adib Shishakli" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adib_al-Shishakli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
